Once upon a time, there was a little girl named Sue. She loved to play and jump and play together. One day, Sue saw the pretty paper and wanted to touch it.
Sue said to the store, "Can I touch the paper, please?" The store man said, "Yes, Sue! I know how to touch it." Sue touched the paper and it was very beautiful.
Sue touched the paper. The paper was big and the same. Suddenly, the paper. Sue was scared and started to cry. Her mom heard her cry. She went to tell her mom and said, "Mom, the paper is big and strong. It's not a toy, but a real bird!" Sue felt better and said, "I just like that, her mom! It's not a toy, but a real bird!"

